WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.578
Host: Explain why a target-gland hormone and
its pituitary signal can move in opposite
directions.

2
00:00:06.578 --> 00:00:14.607
Guide: A target-gland hormone can inhibit its
upstream control signals. When target-gland
secretion falls,

3
00:00:14.607 --> 00:00:19.425
Guide: reduced negative feedback permits the
pituitary signal to rise,

4
00:00:19.425 --> 00:00:23.874
Guide: provided the central components of the
axis remain functional.

5
00:00:23.874 --> 00:00:30.202
Host: Low thyroid hormone is accompanied by a
TSH that is not appropriately elevated.

6
00:00:30.202 --> 00:00:33.421
Host: What does this challenge in a simple
model?

7
00:00:33.421 --> 00:00:37.700
Guide: The assumption that the central
feedback response is intact.

8
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:44.438
Guide: An intact pituitary response to primary
thyroid failure would usually raise TSH;

9
00:00:44.438 --> 00:00:48.002
Guide: central influences merit consideration.
